# NB: apps/fauna-linux and apps/fauna-windows are deliberately NOT ignored — they
# are Rust workspace members (fauna-linux + the six apps/fauna-windows/* crates)
# whose presence the nest-image build now needs so the committed Cargo.lock stays
# canonical for `cargo build --locked` (release-integrity.md S6). The Dockerfile
# rust-native/rust-wasm stages COPY these trees so cargo can resolve the FULL
# workspace; nothing in the nest build graph depends on them, so their source is
# resolved but never compiled and never reaches the runtime image. (ios/android/
# apple stay ignored — Swift/Kotlin, not cargo members.) See the Dockerfile
# comment at the strip's former site for the full rationale.

# The SPA's wasm chunks reach the image ONLY from the rust-wasm stage (the
# Dockerfile COPYs all four files per chunk from it). A long-lived checkout's
# git-ignored static/fauna_wasm* files (a `just wasm` output, panic-witness and
# onnx builds) must not ride along in the `COPY apps/fauna-web/` context: they
# would add files to the web-tree that a clean checkout lacks, and its manifest
# would fail `just web-verify` (release-integrity.md § Web-app verifiability).
apps/fauna-web/static/fauna_wasm*
